-- החלת ההסכם ליישום רפורמת עוז לתמורה בחטיבות העליונות בבתי הספר
-- הממשלתיים (11.11.2013): an exchange of two letters of the same day,
-- registered as a collective agreement (15.1.2014, no. 316/2013). The
-- wages commissioner agrees that the provisions on pay and terms of work
-- of the Oz LaTmura agreement of 14.8.2011 apply to the State's teaching
-- employees in the upper divisions of the government schools — for the
-- part of their employment in the upper division alone; that its
-- provisions on exhaustion of claims and industrial peace apply to them
-- for the period it sets; and that there is no double payment for the
-- public-sector framework agreements. הסתדרות המורים's secretary-general
-- agrees, and both agree to submit the correspondence for registration.
--
-- THE OZ LATMURA AGREEMENT is imported for what the letters apply: its
-- period (§3), its exhaustion of claims (§54) and its industrial peace
-- (§57), whose parties for these teachers are the State and הסתדרות
-- המורים, the parties to the letters. Which of its pay provisions reach a
-- teacher is the Oz agreement's own; the letters decide only who is
-- reached and for what part of his work.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT `oz-founding-3`
IMPORT `oz-founding-54`

§ `החלת ההסכם ליישום רפורמת עוז לתמורה בחטיבות העליונות בבתי הספר הממשלתיים — 11.11.2013`

DECLARE `upper-division letters action` IS ONE OF
    `strike or disrupt work over a matter the Oz agreement settles, as the letters of 11.11.2013 apply it`
    `lock out or disrupt work over a matter the Oz agreement settles, as the letters of 11.11.2013 apply it`
    `submit the letters of 11.11.2013 for registration as a collective agreement`

-- akn:preamble The letter's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The letterhead: the Ministry of Finance; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p2 The letterhead: the wages commissioner; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p3 The registration stamp: registered on 15.1.2014, number 316/2013; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 The Hebrew date; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 The date; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p6 The file mark (שכ. 2013-35955); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p7 "To"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p8 The addressee; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p9 The addressee's post, the union's secretary-general; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p10 The subject line; no rule.

§§ `מכתב הממונה על השכר`

@desc A teaching employee, as far as the letters of 11.11.2013 ask.
DECLARE `upper-division teacher of 11.11.2013` HAS
    `a teaching employee in the State's service, for 11.11.2013` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed in a government school, for 11.11.2013`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc בית ספר ממשלתי
    `the share of his employment in the upper division, for 11.11.2013` IS A NUMBER @desc the part of his employment in the upper division (החטיבה העליונה); the rest, in the junior high school, is outside the letters

-- ¶1: the Oz agreement's provisions on pay and terms of work apply to the
-- State's teaching employees employed in the upper division of the
-- government schools; one who is employed in the junior high school too
-- is reached for the part of his employment in the upper division alone.
@ref akn:hc_1/p1
GIVEN t IS AN `upper-division teacher of 11.11.2013`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the letters of 11.11.2013 apply the Oz agreement to` t IF
        t's `a teaching employee in the State's service, for 11.11.2013`
    AND t's `employed in a government school, for 11.11.2013`
    AND t's `the share of his employment in the upper division, for 11.11.2013` GREATER THAN 0

GIVEN t IS AN `upper-division teacher of 11.11.2013`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the part of the employment the Oz agreement reaches under the letters of 11.11.2013` t IS
    IF `the letters of 11.11.2013 apply the Oz agreement to` t
    THEN t's `the share of his employment in the upper division, for 11.11.2013`
    ELSE 0

-- ¶2: the Oz agreement's provisions on exhaustion of claims (its §54,
-- imported) and industrial peace (its §57) apply to these teachers, for
-- the period it sets (its §3, imported, to 31.12.2016). A claim is
-- exhausted as §54 exhausts it.
@ref akn:hc_1/p2
GIVEN m IS A `matter of an Oz claim`, `the period it is for begins on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a claim of these teachers is exhausted under the letters of 11.11.2013` m `the period it is for begins on` IF
    `exhausted under section 54` m `the period it is for begins on`

-- §57's industrial peace, with the parties to the letters in place of the
-- Oz agreement's own: in the Oz agreement's period, on the matters it
-- settles, neither the State nor הסתדרות המורים takes strike, lock-out or
-- other organised disruption of work against the other.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `a matter the Oz agreement settles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `upper-division letters action`
DECIDE `industrial peace under the letters of 11.11.2013` d `a matter the Oz agreement settles` IS
    IF `in the Oz agreement's period` d AND `a matter the Oz agreement settles`
    THEN (PARTY `the State`
          SHANT `lock out or disrupt work over a matter the Oz agreement settles, as the letters of 11.11.2013 apply it`)
         RAND
         (PARTY `the teachers' union`
          SHANT `strike or disrupt work over a matter the Oz agreement settles, as the letters of 11.11.2013 apply it`)
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ¶3: for these teachers there is no double payment for carrying out the
-- public-sector framework agreements: a framework agreement's cost, which
-- §56 of the Oz agreement applies to its teachers and the State's own
-- agreements apply to them, is paid once.
@ref akn:hc_1/p3
GIVEN `times the framework agreement's cost is paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the letters of 11.11.2013 allow paying a framework agreement` `times the framework agreement's cost is paid` IF
    `times the framework agreement's cost is paid` AT MOST 1

-- akn:hc_1/p4 The commissioner asks for a letter in reply agreeing to this one; a request, which the reply answers.

-- ¶5, and the reply's last paragraph: each side agrees that the
-- correspondence be submitted for registration as a collective agreement
-- — which it was (the stamp). The text sets no day for it (convention
-- dates.no-deadline).
@ref akn:hc_1/p5 akn:att_1__hc_1/p11
`the registration of the letters of 11.11.2013` MEANS
    PARTY `the wages commissioner`
    MAY   `submit the letters of 11.11.2013 for registration as a collective agreement`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:conclusions/p1 The closing greeting; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p2 The signature; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p3 The signatory's name, the wages commissioner; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p4 "Copy"; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p5 The copy's addressee, the Ministry's Director-General; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p6 The ministry's address; no rule.

§§ `מכתב התשובה של מזכ"ל הסתדרות המורים`

-- akn:attachments The annexes' frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 The corpus's note naming the reply; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p2 The Hebrew date; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p3 The date; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p4 "To"; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p5 The addressee; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p6 The addressee's post, the wages commissioner; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p7 The addressee's ministry; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p8 The subject line; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p9 The reference to the commissioner's letter of 11.11.2013; no rule.

-- The secretary-general agrees that the Oz agreement's provisions apply
-- to these teachers, for the part of their employment in the upper
-- division, as the commissioner's letter sets out: the application holds
-- once both letters agree to it.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p10
GIVEN `the union agreed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, t IS AN `upper-division teacher of 11.11.2013`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application of 11.11.2013 is agreed for` `the union agreed in writing` t IF
    `the union agreed in writing` AND `the letters of 11.11.2013 apply the Oz agreement to` t

-- akn:attachments/p1 The closing greeting; no rule.
-- akn:attachments/p2 The signature; no rule.
-- akn:attachments/p3 The signatory's name; no rule.
-- akn:attachments/p4 The signatory's post, secretary-general; no rule.
-- akn:attachments/p5 "Copy"; no rule.
-- akn:attachments/p6 The copy's addressee, the Ministry's Director-General; no rule.
-- akn:attachments/p7 The union's address; no rule.

§§ `examples`

-- A State teacher in a government school, 60% of his employment in the
-- upper division and the rest in the junior high: the Oz agreement
-- reaches the 60%. One employed only in the junior high is not reached.
GIVEN `upper share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `upper-division teacher of 11.11.2013`
DECIDE `a government-school teacher of 11.11.2013` `upper share` IS
    `upper-division teacher of 11.11.2013` WITH
        `a teaching employee in the State's service, for 11.11.2013` IS TRUE
        `employed in a government school, for 11.11.2013`        IS TRUE
        `the share of his employment in the upper division, for 11.11.2013` IS `upper share`

#ASSERT `the part of the employment the Oz agreement reaches under the letters of 11.11.2013` (`a government-school teacher of 11.11.2013` 0.6) EQUALS 0.6
#ASSERT NOT `the letters of 11.11.2013 apply the Oz agreement to` (`a government-school teacher of 11.11.2013` 0)
#ASSERT `industrial peace under the letters of 11.11.2013` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2017) TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `a claim of these teachers is exhausted under the letters of 11.11.2013` `a matter the Oz agreement settles` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2014)
#ASSERT NOT `a claim of these teachers is exhausted under the letters of 11.11.2013` `a matter the Oz agreement settles` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2017)
#ASSERT NOT `the letters of 11.11.2013 allow paying a framework agreement` 2
